     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: ToT for National Resource Person conducted from 13-15 June 2019. (22 Participants)

Roll-out training to BHU-II &amp; sub post staff of 6 eastern districts including DHO&apos;s conducted from 18-23 June 2019. (2 days training in 3 batches) (Total 184 staff, Male 126, Female 58)

Completed in May 2019. 8 District Health Officer from priority districts. 2 FNPH faculty members responsible for pre and in-service training of health assistants (HA) 3 Program Officers of HPD

(12 male and 1 female)

26 HA graduates (10 male, 16 female) of 2019 trained on IPC/BCC in August 2019 with funding support from FNPH

The in-service training held on 22-26 September 2019 (29 participants)

Training for other districts deferred due to COVID-19

Equipment to meet the standards for maintaining vaccine cold chain are procured (Vaccine van &amp; cold chain equipment)

Gender responsive design included in drawing and estimates of satellite clinics including separate OPD toilet.

Civil work packages of Dagana district (W-08) completed on 31 July 2021, Trashigang and Trashiyantse district package (W-05) is ongoing, Mongar district packagec(W-04) are awarded and completed on 27 June 2021. The technical bids evaluation report of Trongsa and Zhemgang package (W-07) is in the process of review and package of Pemagatshel and Samdrup Jongkhar (W-06) under ADB&apos;s review for contract awarding.

Government allocated Nu.500 million on 2 February 2018, vide Cheque no. 010239.

Cabinet order C-3/163/074 dated 12 July 2018 delinks BHTF from RCSC.

BIA published after approval by 48th high level committee meeting held on 8 June 2018.

BHTF recruited all required staff. BHTF has 7 staff in total with 2 female employee (28.6% are women).

BHTF with identified consultants have completed the task and will be endorsed by the new board, however there is a delay due to COVD-19 as the board has not been able to meet. BHTF submitted to BHRM and it is under review.

MOH has received the approval from the Cabinet for onward submission of the health bill for the Parliament session. MOH has submitted to Cabinet

e-Health strategy published after approval by 49th High Level Committee Meeting held on 29 June 2018

Executive order: MoH/PPD/PPMS-25/2018/972 dated 29 June 2018 constitutes the HIS governing body with ToR.

Development of draft enterprise architecture for HIS completed. Finalized and and approved by HIS governing board and MOIC as per executive order DITT/34(8)/2020-21/440 dated 1 December 2020

eHealth Standard has been incorporated into the eGIF as per Executive order DITT/34(8)/2020-21/440 dated 1 December 2020</narrative>
